      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Model links",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen-Image 2.1 - Text to Image\n\n[Qwen-Image 2.1](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1) is Qwen's new unified text-to-image + image-editing model \u2014 just 7B parameters in the visual generation component, smaller than the previous open Qwen image release, with native transparent (RGBA) image support.\n\nThis started from the official ComfyUI Qwen-Image 2.1 workflow (day-one support from the Comfy team). I've added a **GGUF loader path** (for lower-VRAM cards), a **LoRA loader**, and an **upscale** step. Toggle the paths with the Fast Groups Bypasser.\n\n### Models\n- [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (FP8-class base, ~7 GB)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf](https://huggingface.co/Abiray/Qwen-Image-2.1-GGUF/tree/main) (or another quant, ~4-7 GB) -> `models/unet/` (low VRAM path)\n- [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n\nFor even lower VRAM there's also a [w4a8 text encoder](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) (untested here).\n\n### Notes\n- Pick FP8 (default) or a GGUF quant with the bypasser.\n- ~25 steps, 1024x1024. This is a work in progress \u2014 more coming.\n- An image-edit workflow is planned as a follow-up."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Qwen-Image 2.1 - Text to Image\n\n[Qwen-Image 2.1](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1) is Qwen's new unified text-to-image + image-editing model \u2014 just 7B parameters in the visual generation component, smaller than the previous open Qwen image release, with native transparent (RGBA) image support.\n\nThis started from the official ComfyUI Qwen-Image 2.1 workflow (day-one support from the Comfy team). I've added a **GGUF loader path** (for lower-VRAM cards), a **LoRA loader**, and an **upscale** step. Toggle the paths with the Fast Groups Bypasser.\n\n### Models\n- [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (FP8-class base, ~7 GB)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf](https://huggingface.co/Abiray/Qwen-Image-2.1-GGUF/tree/main) (or another quant, ~4-7 GB) -> `models/unet/` (low VRAM path)\n- [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n\nFor even lower VRAM there's also a [w4a8 text encoder](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) (untested here).\n\n### Notes\n- Pick FP8 (default) or a GGUF quant with the bypasser.\n- ~25 steps, 1024x1024. This is a work in progress \u2014 more coming.\n- An image-edit workflow is planned as a follow-up."
      },
